-- 1.2.88 (user: "pause pathing if the player enters combat, use the same route that was calculated after combat has ended; generate pathing more quickly; choose the flattest terrain regardless of added distance"): (1) COMBAT PAUSE: when a fight starts, a running travel walk is stopped and the unwalked rest of its planned path is kept (240 s); the next travel walk to the same destination walks the SAME path from the point nearest the player (within 90 yd) - no new plan, so the walk after a fight starts at once. (2) FLATTEST TERRAIN: a plan of 40-450 yd that climbs / drops more than 0.10 yd per yd walked is walked at once and the via routes round it are asked (both sides, 3 rings in parallel); the route with the least total climbing (not the shortest) that has at most 80% of the plan's climbing replaces it, if the player has moved under 30 yd. Sentinel's own settings are not touched.
