-- 1.2.83 (user: "game closed in combat during facing / combat"; log 17:37:50): The process did not crash (no dump, Wow still running); the CONNECTION dropped - the bot went silent for 28 s with state lines still running, until a loading screen at 17:38:18 - the 8th disconnect of the day. The last second held a 118 degree look-at lock + a cast + a stop / set_target in one frame, and three earlier disconnects also sat within a second of a large turn + a cast. Not proven, but the new facing (1.2.81) snaps a turn instantly. (1) STEPPED TURNS: a turn over 60 degrees is made in steps of 60 degrees (a look-at position 60 degrees round from the CURRENT heading, held 0.3 s), never a single snap. (2) A cast waits for the turn: 0.4 s at most (the facing hold removed in 1.2.64 is back for a target outside the front cone), so a cast is not sent in the same frame as a large turn. (3) nav_stop with nothing to stop is a no-op at most every 0.5 s (it ran ten times a second while waiting for a corpse).
-- 1.2.82 (user: "check and ensure enum collision, LoS and other enums are being used correctly"): ENUM AUDIT. enums.collision_flags are bitmask constants (None, DoodadCollision 0x1, WmoCollision 0x10, Terrain 0x100, EntityCollision 0x100000, LineOfSight 0x100010, combine(...names)). Two uses were wrong: (1) the ray helpers' COLLISION mask ADDED EntityCollision, so a standing mob / NPC / player counted as an obstacle ("an obstacle 0.6 yd high ahead, no progress - jump" could jump over a gnome); (2) their LOS mask OR-ed DoodadCollision onto LineOfSight, so thin collision-only doodads blocked a line the game itself calls clear. Now ONE module (movement/flags.lua) builds the masks for trace.lua and astar.lua: WALK = Doodad|Wmo, GROUND = WALK|Terrain, COLLISION = STATIC = GROUND (world geometry only), LOS = LineOfSight alone; a log line shows them in hex ("collision flags: ..."). Also the unit classification (ESP, smart.tough) and the class ids (mount) are read from enums.classification / enums.class_id, the old numbers only as the fallback. Every other enums.* name the product uses was checked against the live stub: class_id.*, creature_type.CRITTER / HUMANOID, power_type.MANA / RAGE, window_enums.font_id, class_id_to_name - all exist.
-- 1.2.81 (user: "create combat enemy facing logic using this API" - the Movement Handler): COMBAT ENEMY FACING (movement/facing.lua). The player is turned onto the fight's target with movement_handler:look_at_target (a look-at lock, NO movement key) instead of the Simple Movement "face" walk of 1.2.34 (a 1.2 yd walk = key presses). It faces when the target is alive, attackable, within 45 yd and more than 40 degrees off - or at once, any angle, when the client just refused a swing / cast for facing; the lock is 0.5-1.2 s by the size of the turn, never asked again while the same target's lock still runs, never faster than every 0.25 s; the fight's target first, else the nearest hostile attacking the player. A cast of a cast time at an enemy asks cast time + 0.2 s of lock (and a light movement pause while moving) right before it is sent. The lock is let go (unlock_look_at) when the fight ends / a halt / a rest / an unload, and the handler is pumped once per render frame from the render callback (:on_render). The Simple Movement walk stays as the fallback only when the handler cannot be loaded.
