-- 1.2.77 (user: "watch logs for the time Sentinel takes to create paths; find a quicker method"): PLAN LATENCY MEASURED, HEDGED PLANS, NEXT-LEG PREFETCH. The logs of 222 sessions (983 plan requests): when the server answers it is FAST - median 0.05 s, p90 0.10 s, the same for 10 or 400 points; about 7 % (55) got no reply in 3 s and then cost 12-105 s (35 ended in a walk-loop blacklist, 9 got a plan after 22-97 s). So the tail is the problem. (1) HEDGED PLANS: no reply after 0.5 s -> a second request goes out (a far goal: its first 200 yd as a partial plan; a near goal: another mesh floor of it), after 1.3 s a third; the first valid reply wins (the winning alternate floor is remembered), a failed reply waits for the others. (2) PREFETCH: while a leg runs with under 140 yd of path left, the path to the guide's NEXT waypoint is planned from this leg's end; when the guide asks for it the path is there at once ("prefetched path used"). (3) A "plan stats" line every 2 minutes: plans, median / p90 / max latency, hedges and wins, prefetches asked / used.
