-- 1.2.75 (user: "paths should be able to be generated for long distances, 500+ yards at a time, regenerating while the player is running without stopping, by looking ahead"): LONG ROUTES + SPLICED RE-PLANS (movement/nav.lua LONG). (1) ANCHORED PLANS: a goal more than 450 yd away is planned in ONE plan_route request through anchors every 320 yd along the line (each snapped to a mesh floor, none within 150 yd of the goal): the server plans leg by leg, so 500-2000 yd come back in one reply; an anchored plan that fails is asked again plainly; an anchored plan waits 6 s (was 3). (2) PARTIAL PLANS: a plan that ends 80+ yd short of the goal but gets 120+ yd closer is walked as far as it goes and the horizon plans the next stretch 150 yd before the path's end. (3) SPLICED RE-PLANS: the rolling horizon plans from a SPLICE POINT on the running path (speed x (latency + 1 s) ahead, 25-70 yd), and the reply keeps the running path up to that point and continues from it - no backtracking, no stop; a failed splice leaves the running path alone (it used to fall back to a plain move_to). Horizon chain per goal 12 asks (was 6).
-- 1.2.74 (user: "use intelligent gating logic, focusing the memory on each task at hand: generating paths, combat, resting, looting"): TASK-GATED ESP. The ESP reads the bot's task (combat > resting > looting > pathing > idle; a higher task at once, a lower one after 1.5 s) and works on what that task needs. COMBAT: 60 yd every 0.25 s, enemies and packs only (the snapshot shows the task). RESTING: 45 yd; away_vector - the way to sit down is away from ALL the hostiles around, not only the nearest (resting move_away_from). LOOTING: 45 yd; corpse_risk - a corpse with 2+ hostile mobs, an elite or a much higher level within 12 yd is not walked to for 10 s (loot.tick gate, logged once). PATHING: 100 yd; hazards() - camps of 4+ linked mobs, elites and much higher levels join the plan audit (nav N.danger_at: a route round them is asked). IDLE: 100 yd, 1 s. Quest memory is kept for the CURRENT STEP only; quest / node work is skipped in combat, rest and looting.
