-- 1.2.53: ARROW FIELDS LOGGED. The arrow log line now also lists every other field of the arrow table (dist, goal_num, is_manual and anything else Zygor hands over), to find out what a Hearthstone leg looks like to the API: log 11:22-11:24 showed only "type way" while Zygor's own arrow showed the Hearthstone icon.
-- 1.2.52: ZYGOR'S HEARTHSTONE LEG. Zygor's travel router can put a "Hearth to <bind>" leg on its pointer arrow (Hearthstone icon); the bot ignored it and walked 1270 yd (Westfall coast -> Sentinel Hill, steep span with no way round). The bot now uses item 6948 when that leg is the arrow (out of combat, standing still, off cooldown); not carried / on cooldown / not taking = it walks as before. guide.route_title(), TR.route_hearth.
-- 1.2.51: SLOW PATH IS NOT A STALL. Log 10:49 Stormwind: Sentinel sat in awaiting_path for 36 s (server slow); the 30 s no-progress rule restarted the walk twice, resetting the wait. The quest stall clock now waits up to 90 s while Sentinel is still planning the path.
-- 1.2.50: FACING REFUSALS. "You are facing the wrong way!" (40) and "Target needs to be in front of you." (16) came mostly while casting Flame Shock / Lightning Bolt after the turn window (0.8 s) ran out. The client refusal is now remembered for 4 s: the facing check uses a 40 degree cone (was 90) and the turn gets 2.5 s before the cast goes anyway.
-- 1.2.49: MORE AUDIT FIXES. An empty corpse ("There is no loot.", 43 in the logs) ends the loot bursts at it; a target that stays unreachable for 3 min holds its goal (then the 2-minute blocked-goal skip applies). core.input.look_at checked against the live stub.
-- 1.2.48: AUDIT FIXES. Boat back from another continent (an Eastern Kingdoms waypoint read as "same continent" because its continent is 0/unknown, so the boat was never asked for: 90 min stranded in Darkshore after a stuck-hearth); the stuck-hearth learns the bind continent and refuses a hearth that would cross continents; a goal blocked for 2 min requests a step skip; a gear item that would not equip is not retried until the game restarts and the client error is logged; no casts while stunned; the NPC-stuck watchdog stops the bot only after twice the resets; dead movement_handler requires removed.
-- 1.2.47: NO LOGOUT WHILE ALIVE. The 5-minute stuck rule logged a living player out when it had no Hearthstone, the stone was on cooldown or the cast did not take. It now stops the walk, blacklists that destination and carries on; only a ghost logs out.
-- 1.2.46: A SHORT MESH RAMP IS WALKED. Log 09:34: the steep span (rise 3.2 over 2.8 yd, grade 1.14) was the only way out - all 10 side routes crossed it - and the old ladder walked 29 yd then gave the destination up. When no side route is clean, a plan whose steep spans are all short (<= 6 yd), under the client's 1.19 (~50 deg) limit and at most 3 is walked as Sentinel planned it.
-- 1.2.45: A KILL TARGET ON UNCLIMBABLE GROUND IS SKIPPED. Log 09:19-09:28: the Mountain Buzzard step sat at 4/6 for 9 minutes - the closest buzzard was on a ridge whose every route starts with a steep span, the
-- route gave each spot up (11 times, "crosses ground too steep to walk") and the engine kept approaching the next buzzard on the same ridge, then "closing directly" into the cliff. When the approach finds the
-- route "blacklisted" / steep after APPROACH_WAIT, the unit is marked unreachable (state, 45 s, find_mob skips it), combat is released and the next scan picks another target.
-- 1.2.44: SIDE ROUTES: WIDER AND EXPLAINED. The 1.2.39 both-sides detours worked in game (09:15-09:17: a steep span routed around 30 yd out, the supply run reached the inn), but on the ridge at
-- (-5742, -3933) (grade 1.24) every side route failed and the log said nothing about why. A fifth ring at 140 yd is tried, and when no ring is clean the trail says how many via routes were asked and
-- how many had no plan / ended short / were still steep ("plan audit: no way around the steep span ...").
-- 1.2.43: WALK LOOP BREAKER (movement/nav.lua). Log 09:03-09:06: a supply run to an inn 1,100 yd away was re-issued every second (100+ walks) while the player stood on one spot for over two minutes; no walk ran long
-- enough to fail, the stuck ladder and the 5-minute hearth rule need a running walk, and Auto Load then reloaded the plugin. issue_walk now counts the same destination asked LOOP_N (8) times over 6+ s while the
-- player moved under 4 yd: it logs "walk loop: ..." with the Sentinel state, blacklists the destination (r 8) and refuses the walk, so the trip / goal gives up instead of standing still. Combat, lift, boat, swim,
-- portal and A* walks are never counted.
-- 1.2.42: "CAN'T DO THAT WHILE MOVING" GATE THAT FIRES. The 1.2.35 gate (core_castable: cast time > 0 and me:is_moving()) never logged a single "core: moving" refusal while 7 such client errors came in 5 minutes -
-- is_moving answers false the moment after a walk stops. movement.pulse now stamps R.last_move_t (Sentinel walk, Simple Movement turn / kite, back-pedal, the client's is_moving) and a cast-time
-- spell waits spellcheck.STILL_S = 0.3 s after it (movement.recently_moved). The ui_error line for "while moving" now carries what the gate saw (id, cast time, moving, recent).
-- 1.2.41: RAY ERRORS FIXED, 422 LOOP FINISHED. (1) core.graphics.trace_line answers TRUE for a CLEAR line and FALSE for a blocked one (Core_Api graphics.md: "true if there is a valid trace line"; its
-- own example reads true as line of sight). movement/trace.lua and movement/astar.lua read true as a hit, so the self-check (a ray down through the ground, which IS blocked) "hit nothing"
-- five times in every session and "Ray helpers switched off for this session" every time; both now read false as blocked. The self-check still switches the helpers off if the ground under
-- the player ever reads clear. (2) A floor cached by walk_at_floor / retry_at_ground is used however far above the player it is: with two floors at a spot 1.2.40 still clamped every guide
-- tick back to the player's z and Sentinel answered 422 again (log 08:27-08:28).
-- 1.2.40: HTTP 422 "POSITION NOT ON NAVMESH" LOOP (movement/nav.lua). The nav layer read the real mesh floor at a destination (z 405.8 under a hill, 78.3 in Stormwind) and issue_walk then
-- clamped it back to the player's own height ("dest z is 95 yd above the player - walking at z 311.1 (not up the mountain)"): no mesh there, Sentinel answered 422 after ~20 s of retries,
-- again and again. A height read from the mesh (walk_at_floor, retry_at_ground, a cached zfix, or the only floor at the spot) is now never clamped; a 422 "not on navmesh" goes through the
-- same floor retry / local search as "unreachable".
-- 1.2.39: ROUTE AROUND STEEP GROUND, EITHER DIRECTION (movement/nav.lua). When the plan audit still finds a steep span after the zone replans, Sentinel is asked (plan_route with a via
-- node) for routes beside the span on BOTH sides, perpendicular to the climb, 15 / 30 / 55 / 90 yd out, nearest ring first; each answer is slope-audited, the shorter clean one at a ring is
-- walked with follow_path ("routed around it on the left / right"). Nothing clean: the old ladder (audited prefix, then the give-up) as before. Sentinel still plans and walks.
-- 1.2.38: WAYPOINT READING AUDIT (312 logged sessions). Zygor writes a step's |goto on ONE line; the other goals on the same NPC / object read "0 waypoints": every click goal,
-- every talk goal, 17 of 143 turn-ins, 21 of 186 accepts. Cost: ~1,900 "no usable waypoint" ticks (Waterlogged Axe / Saw / Toolbox, Sacks of Oats, Lay / Fall of Ameth'Aran) and 120 s
-- searches at "talk Ariena Stormfeather" before an fpath line and "talk Innkeeper Allison" before a home line. An NPC / object goal (talk gossip accept turnin click clicknpc vendor
-- trainer stablemaster home buy bank) with no point of its own now takes the first later point of the same step (q collect get accept turnin fpath ferry home buy bank goto, or a
-- coordinates-only line); a different NPC starting, or other work (kill, use), ends the scan. A quest line whose quest has every objective finished waits for Zygor to tick it
-- instead of pausing as "unknown" (step 62 stalled, Auto Load reloaded the plugin every 5 minutes).
-- 1.2.37: HEARTH TO A CITY INN. (1) After a Hearthstone to Stormwind the supply run walked 862 yd to Goldshire with the Pig and Whistle innkeeper 30 yd away:
-- supplies.nearest_inn now also asks merchants.nearest_inn (innkeepers seen) and takes the nearer. (2) The hearth "find" stage tried the nearest 8 / 12 NPCs in
-- order (guards, citizens) and gave up at "found no merchant nearby" with the innkeeper and eight repairers in range; it now tries NPCs flagged vendor (0x80) or,
-- for a repair trip, repair (0x1000) first.
-- 1.2.36: WATER BUYING OFF THE EASTERN KINGDOMS, FULL RESTS. supplies.nearest_inn read only the Eastern Kingdoms inn list, so in Darkshore a food / water run
-- found "no inn or innkeeper known here" and a shaman with no water sat at 0 mana; it now falls back to merchants.nearest_inn, the innkeepers the bot has
-- seen on this continent (Auberdine's Innkeeper Shaussiy). A rest out of combat now runs to full (REST_DONE and REST_TOPUP 99.5, was 90 / 95). The plan
-- audit's steep-span line carries the span's rise, length, grade and position.
-- 1.2.35: NO CASTS THE CLIENT REFUSES. spellcheck.core_castable refuses a cast-time spell while the player is moving ("Can't do that while moving") and a cast on a dead target ("Your target is dead"); opts.allow_moving skips the first.
-- 1.2.34: FACING AND KEEPING ENEMIES IN FRONT THROUGH SIMPLE MOVEMENT, every class (movement/front.lua). A target more than 40 degrees
-- off the facing is turned on with a short Simple Movement walk (look_at system, 1.2 yd, not while casting, at most 1/s); an enemy behind
-- the player makes a kite of up to 6 yd toward Sentinel's flee point. process() runs every frame while a move is active; Sentinel stays
-- stopped and nav refuses other walks while it does. Travel is still Sentinel's. movement.face (all call sites) now goes through it.
-- 1.2.33: BOAT WAIT WHERE THE PLAYER STANDS. In Stormwind (within 250 yd of the harbor) the bot waits for the ship at the player's
-- own position instead of walking to the map-icon dock; farther away it walks to the dock first. Ships at the harbor count too.
-- 1.2.32: BOAT STORMWIND <-> DARKSHORE (movement/boat.lua). A Zygor goal on the other continent (Darkshore from the Eastern Kingdoms,
-- or back to Stormwind) is a boat run: walk to the dock, wait for the ship (a Transport game object), board it once it stands still at
-- the dock, ride (nothing else moves the player), step off when it stands still at the other dock; the reverse is the same machine.
-- Docks come from the Forever client's tables: AreaPOI Stormwind Harbor (-8573.5, 990.1), GameObjects 'Boat to Stormwind' at
-- Auberdine (6509.2, 799.2, 8.2). A ship that lands at another dock is left there and the normal walk goes on.
-- 1.2.31: the option moved to the Spells tab.
-- 1.2.30: AVOID OTHER PLAYER TARGETS (Spells tab, off by default). When ticked, a mob another player is fighting is never picked:
-- its own target is a player that is not you, your party or your pet, or a visible player in combat has it targeted. A mob on you is
-- still fought. Applied to the grind scan (targeting.scan_enemies) and to the quest guide's fightable check.
-- 1.2.29: FULL BAGS THE COUNT MISSED. Log 17:08-17:15: loot came back "empty after 3 loot request(s)" while the bot counted 5-6 free
-- slots and never went to a vendor. When the client says "inventory is full" (UI error) within 90 s, bags count as full until a vendor trip
-- completes (ignored for 120 s after one). The bags line now lists each bag's used/capacity, and the client's UI error lines go to the
-- action log (event/ui_error), so a wrong count can be seen.
-- 1.2.28: ENEMIES IN FRONT + FLEEING MOBS. In position with a fighting enemy more than 110 degrees off the player's facing
-- (behind it) within 12 yd, combat movement kites away from all of them on Sentinel's flee path for 2 s (at most every 6 s), so the
-- followers trail in front when the player turns on the target. A melee class (warrior, paladin, rogue, shaman, druid) whose
-- target runs (1.5 yd/s away, or 0.5 when wounded) chases at once - no chase gap, re-path at 1 yd - and holds the GUI melee distance.
-- 1.2.27: NO MORE 11 HOURS ON ONE STEP. A step with no actionable goals, or a use goal with no verified item, is skipped
-- with Zygor's skip_current_step after 30 s (retried every 60 s; the note says to load the next guide when Zygor refuses).
-- A use goal with no item id uses the ONE usable quest item in the bags (two or more stay ambiguous).
-- 1.2.26: an unusable quest object (Duskwood Waterlogged Toolbox, underwater) is skipped 5x longer after each give-up instead of every
-- 60 s; buff totems (Strength of Earth, Windfury, Grace of Air) are not dropped on a mob under 55 % health.
-- 1.2.25: MANA + LOGGING. Lightning Shield is not recast in a fight under 50 % mana (it was recast every ~20 s: 100 % -> 1 % mana in one
-- two-mob pull, then 5 deaths in the Tunnel Rat cave); the opening Earthbind needs 50 % mana. New combat/snap line every 3 s of a fight:
-- own hp / mana, target, enemies near, shields, totems per slot.
-- 1.2.24: SHAMAN SETUP FROM THE WOWHEAD FOREVER LEVELING GUIDE. Water Shield (408510) is kept up first, Lightning Shield (10432) is the
-- fallback; Flametongue Weapon (16342) is the default imbue and Windfury Weapon (16362) is off (Flametongue + Windfury Totem is stronger).
-- 1.2.24 (cont.): SPELLS TAB + FIRE NOVA. Totems get their own section (Fire / Earth / Water / Air, purpose beside each, 'out' when it stands,
-- live slot summary on top). Forever's Fire Nova is a spell (408345), not 'Fire Nova Totem': it sat under Other known spells and never cast;
-- it is now a damage spell used with a fire totem out and an enemy within 8 yd (3+ enemies, or 45 % mana).
-- 1.2.23: RACIALS IN COMBAT + MELEE FILLER. Stoneform is used at the start of every fight (was: only under 50 % health with a
-- bleed), War Stomp with one enemy in melee (was two), Gift of the Naaru under 80 % (was 50), mana racials under 60 % (was 30),
-- offensive racials until the target is at 25 % (was 40). Lightning Bolt is also the filler next to a mob when mana is 40 % or
-- more, instead of 3-5 s of nothing cast while Earth Shock cools down.
-- 1.2.22: NO STEEP ROUTES FOR THE LIVING. A route that starts on steep ground is no longer handed to Sentinel for a living player
-- (19:27 log: 340 yd of navigating.recovering, then stuck at a cliff); the goal is refused and blacklisted at once. The same steep
-- span blocking a goal twice (was three times) also gives it up. Only a ghost on a corpse run is still handed to Sentinel.
-- 1.2.21: OPENING SET. The first seconds of a fight drop Fire Nova Totem (fire slot, now ticked by default; not near a crowd-controlled
-- enemy) and Earthbind Totem (earth slot, ahead of Stoneskin; not on a slowed / immune target), then the water / air opening totem follows.
-- Fire Nova's pack rule now ranks below Magma. Only learned, ticked totems are used.
-- 1.2.20: ROLLING RE-PLAN ONLY WHEN STUCK. The 25 s re-plan replaced healthy walks and made Sentinel stop and recover each time (log
-- 18:50-18:58, eight stalls). A long walk that covered 15 yd or more in the last 25 s is left alone; only a slower one is planned again.
-- 1.2.19: STEEP ROUTES GIVEN UP. When the same steep ground (within 25 yd) blocks the same goal three times in 10 minutes - an audited
-- prefix walked, planned again, the same span; or Sentinel hand-offs that ended recovering - the goal is blacklisted for a while and
-- the walk is refused, so callers pick another target instead of trying a route the player cannot cross. Never for a ghost corpse run.
-- 1.2.18: LOOT WALK DURING A MEAL. A corpse walk started 3 s into a rest sat 104 s on the same spot (the rest locks movement; log 18:29-18:31).
-- Looting no longer starts while the player is eating / drinking, and the rest-first clock restarts after a 30 s gap.
-- 1.2.17: SHAMAN OPENING TOTEM + MELEE WHEN DRY. The first 8 s of every fight drop one enabled totem (damage / defense / buff / spell /
-- mana) whatever the mob, if mana is above the floor and the target is within 25 yd and healthy. Out of mana (under 20 %, until 35 %)
-- the engage distance is melee (4 yd): a fleeing mob is chased and the weapon keeps swinging instead of waiting at spell range.
-- 1.2.16: SHAMAN TOTEMS. Earthbind (control) no longer outranks the enabled Stoneskin / Strength of Earth totems when health is under
-- 60 % (it took the single earth slot for 45 s), and Stoneclaw / Healing Stream / Mana Tide may replace ANY catalog totem of ours
-- in their slot, recognised by name (the log: no Stoneclaw at 4 % health because Earthbind sat in the slot). Opt-in utility, resist and
-- cleanse totems we did not place are still never overwritten.
-- 1.2.15: THREAT RANGE + REST. The loot walk and a walking vendor trip now fight a mob whose threat range is on the path (as
-- the quest walk already did) instead of running into it. A corpse more than 60 yd away is not walked to (Stop / Start sent the bot
-- 130-170 yd back to old kills), and a hurt player (health under 45 % or mana under 25 %) rests before walking to a corpse that is
-- not within 15 yd (for at most 20 s, so a player with nothing to eat still loots).
-- 1.2.14: WEAPON UPGRADES. Auto Equip and Auto Equip Weapons are ON by default (they were off), the pause between two weapon-slot
-- equips is 8 s (was 30), and a usable weapon that is not an upgrade logs equip/keep with both item levels.
-- 1.2.13: LONG WALKS REACH THE GOAL. A plan whose first steep span is at the start no longer ends the walk (the 17:38 corpse
-- run stood still after 107 yd): Sentinel plans and walks that leg itself. A long walk (60 yd+) is also planned again from where
-- the player stands every 25 s ("rolling re-plan"), on top of the path-horizon re-ask.
-- 1.2.12: PATH + LOOT. The path horizon no longer replaces an audited-prefix segment mid-walk (a new path every 1-2 s, only
-- 9-20 yd walked per plan). A vendor trip that is only walking no longer switches looting off, so a kill is looted at once instead
-- of "gave up after 30 s"; a queued corpse that is not being looted logs why (loot: N corpse(s) queued, not looting: ...).
-- 1.2.11: LOG-WATCH FIXES. Passive spells (Big Game Hunter, Artisan's Precision, Gardening) are never cast and a spell that
-- 'cast' is not retried for 120 s (59 casts in 20 min). Shaman damage spells stop below 20% mana (resume at 35%) so a
-- low-mana fight is melee, not a Lightning Bolt at 3% mana. A kill goal with no waypoint walks back to the camp remembered
-- from earlier in the run. Zygor step flip-flops (A,B,A inside 5 s) are logged as guide/step_flip.
-- 1.2.10: LONG PATHS. A steep span anywhere on a long plan used to reject the whole plan (action log 2026-11-15 17:02:
-- "plan rejected: unsafe slope", a 1510 yd corpse run: no walk, the player stood still, a request every 5 s). The steep
-- span is still never walked, but the audited prefix before it is (follow_path of the safe points), then the rest is
-- planned again from where it ends; a wall within 12 yd of the start is still refused. Up to 80 segments per goal.
-- 1.2.9: scan the generated path plus enemy threat radii, prioritize the
-- first threat boundary entered, and reject different-floor encounters.
-- 1.2.8: reject unsafe slopes before following planned/recorded paths;
-- require actual planned waypoints and validate local planner endpoint/shortcut grades.
-- 1.2.7: prioritize the combat enemy with lowest remaining HP; preserve
-- Shaman facing during casts and omit self-heal facing preparation.
-- 1.2.6: indoor quest travel preserves destination Z, rejects wrong-floor arrival,
-- and does not substitute cached/alternate floors or skip blocked indoor route points.
-- 1.2.5: combat survival totems outrank routine setup across slots and remain eligible
-- while moving through the normal cast gate. Preserve expiring utility/elemental totems.
-- Successful drops record slot, purpose, health, mana and position in the action log.
-- Forever Shaman scans probe missing starter ranks with live ownership checks.
-- Enabled utility/resistance/cleansing totems provide proactive combat coverage.
-- 1.2.4: preserve live interaction heights through Sentinel; hold failed goals without
-- skipping their siblings immediately; after 5 active minutes without progress, skip the step.
-- Skip positively completed goals and distinguish blocked access from failed interactions.
-- Completion waits name missing objectives and hold after 120 s without progress.
-- Diagnostics separate passive instructions and track movement progress and request IDs.
-- Shaman chooses known, enabled, affordable totems by slot, danger and fight value;
-- emergency replacements preserve manual utility and elemental totems.
-- 1.2.3: a kill goal with no point of its own (action log 2026-11-15, step 137 "kill Frostmane Seers": the player stood at
-- the previous NPC) borrows the collection camp through click / goto lines and otherwise walks to Zygor's arrow.
-- 1.2.2: WAIT AT NPC is a setting. Questing tab slider "Wait at NPC for an unfinished task (s)" (5 - 120, default 20)
-- sets how long the bot stays at a quest NPC, or at a goal whose NPC / object is not in sight, before it asks Zygor
-- to skip the step or moves to the next goal. It never sits the whole time out: a turn-in hold is released the
-- moment the quest is complete, and the not-complete check runs every tick.
-- 1.2.1: a turn-in whose quest is in the log but not complete no longer freezes the bot (log 2026-11-15, step 116
-- "turn in Beer Basted Boar Ribs": "not ready to hand in yet (quest log), waiting" for ever, 300 yd from the NPC).
-- The action log records the quest's missing objectives (quest/turnin_not_ready); after 20 s Zygor is asked to skip
-- the step, and if it refuses the goal is held so the step's other goals are worked.
-- 1.2.0: SHAMAN TOTEMS by element slot and purpose (data/class_spells.lua lists all 25 vanilla/TBC totems; rotations/shaman.lua
-- rules: Searing in a fight worth it, Magma for 2+ enemies, Stoneskin / Stoneclaw by health and enemies on you, Mana Spring /
-- Mana Tide / Healing Stream by mana and health, melee buffs only for an Enhancement build; one totem per slot, a live
-- totem of another kind is never overwritten, a left-behind totem is dropped again). AUTO-EQUIP: profession tools (Mining
-- Pick, Skinning Knife, Blacksmith Hammer, Arclight Spanner, fishing poles) are never equipped as weapons; skipped items
-- are action-log events, not console lines.
-- 1.1.1: ACTION LOG REVIEW (read from a live session file). log/env now carries the game, map, class and level (the
-- header had env {}); ctx has hp, mana, target, step and numeric pos; trail events use their first word as ev
-- (loot/queued, act/engage, nav/move_to ...); the status line is recorded once (the duplicate "note" trail is
-- gone); nav/arrived and nav/walk_failed carry x, y, z, mode and seconds; stall/status_stale flags a running bot
-- whose status has not changed for 20 s; the kill/collect patrol sets its own status ("patrolling for ...")
-- instead of leaving the last loot note up for 50 s.
-- 1.1.0: ACTION LOG + fixes (ported from zygor_questing 1.75.0). actlog.lua writes JSON Lines to
-- scripts_log/mfz_actions/ for Claude to read; errorlog / debuglog write through it and the six
-- logging boxes are replaced by "Action log (for Claude)", "Action log: verbose" and the Questing
-- tab's "Mark moment". Questing tab buttons (Vendor, Skip Goal, Clear Skipped) are the tab head,
-- drawn above the controls. A click goal with no waypoint (log 2026-11-15: Felix's Box, Fallen Logs)
-- searches the object list and, after 120 s, asks Zygor to skip or holds the goal. "Eat/drink skipped"
-- warns once per kind per 2 minutes (was 8 a second). The item-info field dumps are one event.
-- 1.0.0: first release. WoW Forever only (launcher card 8). The quest layer
-- (quest/guide, engine, npc, done, travel, bagstart, diag) reads the live
-- Zygor Guides Viewer (Forever edition) through core.addons.zygor; no
-- RestedXP read exists anywhere in this product. Movement, combat, loot, death,
-- vendor, trainer and the GUI come from the Forever Questing tree and drive
-- the shared Sentinel Navigation client through movement/sentinel.lua only.
